---
# The negative test for networkpolicy.yaml.j2: a pod inside the fence must not reach daniel-server.
#
# INVERTED ON PURPOSE — this Job SUCCEEDS when the connection FAILS. Written the other way round,
# a fence that was never applied would look like a passing test, which is the exact thing this
# rules out. Same shape as n8n-netpol-probe, and for the same reason.
#
# TWO CONTROLS, because one is not enough — learned the hard way on 2026-08-07. The first version
# of this probe tested port {{ container_item.port }} on daniel-server and reported "fence ok".
# It proved nothing: the Docker sonarr publishes NO host port (it is reachable only through
# Traefik), so that connection fails whether the policy exists or not. A DNS control cannot catch
# that — the pod's network stack was fine; the target was simply never reachable.
#
#   1. DNS resolves          -> this pod has a working network stack (checked here)
#   2. the target IS reachable from an UNFENCED pod -> netpol-control-job.yaml.j2, run first
#
# Hence port {{ sonarr_k8s_fence_probe_port }}: Traefik on daniel-server, which is genuinely
# listening on the LAN, so "unreachable" can only be the policy.
#
# It carries the fence label but NOT app=sonarr, so the policy selects it while sonarr's Service
# does not.
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: sonarr-netpol-probe
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  activeDeadlineSeconds: 120
  backoffLimit: 0
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: sonarr-netpol-probe
        netfence: {{ sonarr_k8s_fence_label }}
    spec:
      restartPolicy: Never
      enableServiceLinks: false
      containers:
        - name: probe
          image: {{ sonarr_k8s_probe_image }}
          command:
            - sh
            - -c
            - |
              if ! nslookup kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local >/dev/null 2>&1; then
                echo "CONTROL FAILED: DNS does not resolve from inside the fence, so this probe"
                echo "proves nothing about the policy — a pod with no network would pass it."
                exit 1
              fi
              echo "control ok: DNS resolves, so this pod has a working network stack"
              if nc -w 5 -z {{ k8s_bridge_client_ip }} {{ sonarr_k8s_fence_probe_port }}; then
                echo "FENCE NOT ENFORCED: reached {{ k8s_bridge_client_ip }}:{{ sonarr_k8s_fence_probe_port }}"
                echo "from inside the fence. The rehearsal copy can reach the LAN, which means it"
                echo "can reach the live qbittorrent and the indexers. Do NOT leave sonarr running."
                exit 1
              fi
              echo "fence ok: {{ k8s_bridge_client_ip }}:{{ sonarr_k8s_fence_probe_port }} unreachable from inside it"
          securityContext:
            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
            capabilities:
              drop: ["ALL"]
          resources:
            requests:
              cpu: 10m
              memory: 16Mi
            limits:
              cpu: 200m
              memory: 64Mi
